{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180451-a-brave-new-world","id":1180451,"title":"A Brave New World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-29T10:28:03-08:00","id":1180451,"title":"A Brave New World","content":"With Scion 2nd Ed just around the corner, I have decided to dust off an old idea I had for a Scion Chronicle and see how I could adapt it to the new version of the game.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe core concept of the chronicle is that the War between the Gods and the Titans heats up to such a degree that not even the Gods are uncertain they will be victorious and fear that humanity will suffer greatly should they fall. To that end, the Pantheons decide to work together to create an Ark... a means to preserve a portion of humanity and their own cultures to reseed the world should the worst come to pass.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis Ark will be a single city that the Pantheons have chosen... where they will guide a portion of their followers to (or already have representatives of). Each Pantheon will also send at least one Heroic Scion to help protect the city from Titan influence as it is prepared for its destiny (most notably the PCs). Other Scions will also be drawn to the city... either by fate, their divine parents or their own curiosity... with the end result being nearly every God from the major Pantheons being represented to some degree. Not all will be working for the same goal... some may even try to usurp the project so that only their Pantheon and Culture will be preserved.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs the PCs gain legend and approach the Demigod Tier, the War with the Titans starts to become more apparent to even the most clueless mortal... and the final failsafe is enacted... separating the city from the world in its own little Realm. Only the PC Scions (and maybe some of their closest allies) will be within the city when this happens. The city will only remain in this pocket realm for a short time... days to a month at most... but when the it is returned to the World... everything changes.<br /> <br /> \u200bUpon their return to the world, the Scions and those within the city will find that the rest of the World is very different from what they remember. It is clearly apparent that the Titans were able to break free of their prisons... at least for a while as the physical world has been drastically altered in many ways... but it doesn't appear that the Titans won the war as they seem dormant for the most part. Likewise, it is apparent that the Pantheons of the past have fallen... as they no longer respond as they once did... but neither did they entirely loose as it seems they managed to render the Titans dormant. The PCs, now Demigods will explore this strange new World to try to piece together what happened and what the current state of affairs are between the Gods and the Titans... are they both gone... or merely dormant? As they explore they will also encounter other threats... new and old ones. Some of the other Scions they once knew from their past have managed to survive whatever changed the world... and not all of them will be happy with the returned Scions (especially if the PCs thwarted their plans or left them behind with the city was taken out of time). Their city will not be the only survivors of what happened... other communities will have survived or risen in the years (centuries?) since the city vanished... possibly helped by some of the surviving Scions that were not in the city when it disappeared.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs the PCs approach the God Tier, they will discover the price that the Pantheons and the Titans paid for their war... and just how it was reshaped into what they discovered. They will also discover what remnants of both sides remain... and that their old grudges aren't entirely forgotten or forgiven. It will be up to the PCs to decide where their loyalties will lay... with what remains of the Pantheons of the past and the old rivalries... or if a new path for a new world must be forged. Ultimately, this will see the rise of New Pantheons of New Gods rising to shape a New World from what remains of the one that came before.<br /> <br /> That is the gist of the Chronicle... where the Scions will be dealing with the signs that something will soon happen (Origin), be a part of the preparations for what will happen (Hero), shape the destiny of a city and at least a portion of the world (Demigod) and finally take their place as their own Pantheon to determine the fate of the world (God). Exactly how this will all play out remains to be seen... but for now I am curious as to what others think of this concept and progression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T12:51:55-08:00","id":1180476,"title":"","content":"I approve of the concept of the old pantheons being replaced by a new generation of Scions and bringing about massive changes in the World. It's an idea that I've been having myself for quite a while now. However, I'm on the fence about the Titans being missing in action. If the gods are the embodiment of human concepts, the Titans are the embodiment of natural concepts. Their avatars are merely proxies through which to carry out their machinations. They are the universe personified, which is why the gods can't just kill them. Last time they tried it, they brought an end to the ice age and flooded the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T19:21:55-08:00","id":1180574,"title":"","content":"They aren't missing in action... rather more or less dormant. However, that doesn't mean that their Titanspawn aren't active in this new world.<br /> <br /> \u200bThroughout the Demigod portion of this idea, the PCs will be searching the world for what happened during their disappearance... what actually happened to the old Pantheons... and the Titans. They will find remnants of the old Pantheons... most notably other Scions that have survived and become demigods and Titanspawn that remain loyal to their old masters... but as their legends approach the God Tier, they will discover what just what happened to the world... why the old Pantheons have mostly been caught off from the world and why most of the Titans were rendered dormant... and that what happened isn't finished with the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhile this might be giving things away, my intent is for the PCs to discover that while they were away, the war between the Gods and the Titans attracted the attention of the Primordials... though whether this was deliberate or accidental is undeterminable. Much like when fleas attract the attention of the animal upon which they live, the Primordials swatted at the irritation that the Gods and Titans caused... shattering both sides and restructuring the world. While this has caused nearly all the Titans to become dormant, that doesn't mean they are dead or missing. The same is true for the old Pantheons... their access to the World may have been shattered (and likely many of their members killed), but a remnant of their glory will remain.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the Titans... much like when the Primordials first left their imprint in creation, their actions will cause new Titans to rise... some from the dormant remains of the old Titans... others newly formed from the event that changed the world. At the point in time when the PCs return to the World, it is still in transition as the new Titans have yet to fully form or influence the surviving Titanspawn (some of which believe they can revive their masters from dormancy... though whether such a Titan would be the old one or a new one born from the old is uncertain). This will give the PCs and other Scions the time they need to grow their power to the God Tier where they can take on these newly emerging Titans on more equal footing... fighting them as the old Pantheons once did... or finding a way to keep them dormant... or some other means to deal with them.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut the new and old Titans will not be the only thing the PCs will have to deal with. There will be other bands of Scions that are also nearing the God Tier... forming their own Pantheons to aid their own cultures that may not be friendly with them (especially if the PCs were rivals or antagonistic with them before hand). There will also be the surviving remnants of the old Pantheons... that have finally reconnected with the World... many of which may demand the new Pantheons dissolve and rebuild their old loyalties. Do the PCs do as they are told and forget the friends and allies they have made to rebuild the old Pantheons... or do they defy their parents and form their own Pantheon and fight to make the world what they believe it should be? Will old rivals become new allies and friends... or bitter enemies out to wipe all memory of the PCs deeds from history?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat will be the Legends the PCs leave for this brave new world to remember?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T16:53:50-08:00","id":1181519,"title":"","content":"I'd simply have the chosen Scions sent by their divine superiors to the ark city. Mind you, I'd make the ark city up out of many different cities. The mythic theme would be the city as &quot;The Place of Man.&quot; Perhaps they should have a mentor with them, a goddess bound to the city. Citia crowned with her towers would be what the Romans called her. Like the &quot;Prisoner of London&quot; she'd be physically restricted to the city but be able to travel in time within those boundaries. Thus, outside the city, they'd be on their own, as Citia would be protecting her people and the physical fabric of her city, they'd need to watch out for themselves in town too, but they'd have an ally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-01-2018, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}